{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"c508a36340b54f42f9744baf0bf5f478ac6e2a350d1041bde01468f44fe554c3","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_2962c0630a51e59ade0760c1312c11ae44d5e59d652a7160b2fe2fbc95ebbd08","overall_assessment":"The paper presents a coherent methodological framework that integrates a neural causality detector with a regularized predictive model. The technical formulation is consistent, and the experimental design includes appropriate baselines and statistical reporting. However, the reliance on a single expert for causal ground truth and the lack of code availability limit the verifiability and reproducibility of the results.","paper_id":"ByW2Avqgg","paper_identity_sha256":"2257a9b71a7c08a220255fc4f7f25363a7c0ecfe765e09297499ffa4d5923f4d","prompt_identity_sha256":"881eb47535942e4b4fff2aea07537107d4a64600affb3e8d1e67dd76f87168bf","raw_response_sha256":"b1cc849e4476675bd6ec72e3b4e3ceadec59c4304c129632be2c15b60f01a1e8","request_identity_sha256":"ee31bb938f59d2d5cf4215e1b3296bd200d4b1e9f8036c7992dc0339d28467cf","reviewer_identity_sha256":"c1cd7c7fdd4a2cbeb45c2f21af982ad0f30bffae8ae148e3eba36479685cf360","role":"QUAL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"a31664a11a196d4237787e6d45705c4612ce4a1da033a89b623cd9121ea7dd34","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-013","SRC-014","SRC-015","SRC-021","SRC-022","SRC-025"],"review_text":"The proposed method is technically sound and well-formulated. The paper clearly defines the Independence of Mechanisms (ICM) assumption and uses it to construct a generative model for causal links. The causal regularizer is mathematically consistent, defined as a decomposable regularizer that integrates with both linear and non-linear models. The non-linear model in Equation 2 is a valid extension of logistic regression that allows for input-dependent coefficients, which is a reasonable approach for capturing complex causal relationships. No major conceptual or implementation errors are apparent in the described methodology.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-MET"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-030","SRC-031","SRC-033","SRC-036","SRC-037"],"review_text":"The experimental design is adequate for the claims made. The authors use two large-scale electronic health record datasets (Sutter Health and MIMIC III) with a substantial number of variables and patients. The evaluation includes both predictive performance (AUC, F1) and causal performance (expert-labeled causality scores). The comparison against L1-regularized logistic regression and a two-step procedure provides a fair baseline. The ablation of the causal regularizer's impact on predictive performance is well-documented, showing that the method does not significantly hurt accuracy while improving causal relevance.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-EXP"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-019","SRC-029","SRC-032"],"review_text":"The paper provides sufficient detail for reproduction of the core methodology, including the synthetic data generation process, the structure of the neural network classifier, and the training details for the predictive model. The hyperparameters for the causal detector and the predictive model are described, and the dataset splits are clearly defined. However, the paper does not mention the availability of code, which is a common best practice for reproducibility. The reliance on a single clinical expert for causal labeling is a limitation, as it introduces subjectivity and does not allow for inter-rater reliability assessment.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-REP"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-006","SRC-012","SRC-023"],"review_text":"The paper sufficiently compares its method against relevant prior work, including L1-regularized logistic regression and a two-step causal variable selection procedure. The authors also discuss the relationship to existing causality detection algorithms (e.g., Chalupka et al., 2016; Lopez-Paz et al., 2016) and clarify how their causal regularizer extends these methods. The literature review is comprehensive, covering both causal inference and regularization techniques. The comparison design is fair, using the same datasets and evaluation metrics across all methods.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-CMP"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-033","SRC-036"],"review_text":"The statistical rigor is appropriate for the type of analysis presented. The authors report mean and standard deviation for predictive performance metrics over ten runs, which provides a measure of variance. The causal performance is evaluated using expert-labeled scores, which is a qualitative but reasonable approach for causal validation in the absence of ground truth. However, the paper does not include confidence intervals or significance tests for the causal scores, which would strengthen the statistical validation. The reliance on a single expert for labeling is a limitation, as it does not account for inter-rater variability.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-STA"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"5d3c79ea5f32e61b58d278704534658ecca25a5939cdcd7ebb4afb23367fa51e","paper_id":"ByW2Avqgg","paper_ordinal":72,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"b1cc849e4476675bd6ec72e3b4e3ceadec59c4304c129632be2c15b60f01a1e8","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"ByW2Avqgg","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"2ee74cda42801653fdee96dcca4b097d80e17145e836b79d19589d765b573409","request_identity_sha256":"ee31bb938f59d2d5cf4215e1b3296bd200d4b1e9f8036c7992dc0339d28467cf","role":"QUAL","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v5","usage":{"completion_tokens":1021,"prompt_tokens":18835,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":19856},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"ee31bb938f59d2d5cf4215e1b3296bd200d4b1e9f8036c7992dc0339d28467cf","role":"QUAL","role_ordinal":0,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}